X:1
T:In a Mellow Tone
C:Duke Ellington, 1939
N:Ellington's band recorded it in 1940; Milt Gabler added the words later.
N:Melody and chords from a Real Book transcription (trillian.mit.edu,
N:song/In_a_mellow_tone) in A-flat, checked against a flute MIDI on
N:hamienet.com (track 352501627339274): every pitch agrees. Moved down a
N:minor third to F. Form A B A C, with the two A sections under one repeat.
N:The last bar is one eighth so the loop pays back the pickup.
